@guinnesschen Have this in my Open-source Ghostty based Codex alternative for a while now @ghostex_dev

You can have any Agent call any other agent (Ex. Codex prompting Claude for design + reading response)

Please give it a try 🙏🏻 https://t.co/s0TVb9VPT6

@aleksanderllada @guinnesschen This is how I use different models and agents:
Claude audits Codex's plan. Codex builds. Claude fixes OpenClaw. OpenClaw runs.
Claude became my middleware and auditor.

@guinnesschen Been doing that for a while now, but honestly had a better experience letting Claude do the management part, and Codex be the workhorse.

Codex is just too concise. It saves tokens, but the tasks it delegates don't carry all the context.

https://t.co/sK0GkzrugH

@guinnesschen 4 windows on the same codebase, every day for months.

Search and organize, yeah. But auto-pin worries me.

The window I almost forget about is the one hiding the bug. Auto-pin would never surface it.

